<PARA INFOID = "T030082A100" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "18Aug2005"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Gear Train</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The U660E automatic transaxle uses 2 planetary gear units on the input shaft, a lightweight, compact Ravigneaux type planetary gear and a UD (underdrive) planetary gear, to provide 6 forward speeds and 1 reverse speed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The adoption of the Ravigneaux type planetary gear has greatly simplified and lightened the gear train mechanism located on the intermediate shaft, reducing the weight of the entire unit and the inertial weight of the gear train mechanism. In addition, clutch-to-clutch control has been adopted as the hydraulic control mechanism, reducing the number of shift elements such as one-way clutches and brakes and achieving class-leading light weight and compactness.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a3810098p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "6.389in" />
</FIGURE>

<MECA ID = "T030082A100Kd17" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "1May2007"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
